  "body": "Tender: Closes on Wednesday 9 December 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nWelcome to 16 Lake Road. A beautifully renovated home tucked away along a quiet slip road, where the setting feels more like a little lane. Set on a 642m² freehold section, this private and peaceful home offers thoughtful design, beautiful materials, and space to truly enjoy life.\r\n\r\nWith heritage-inspired design, the interiors bring together warm wooden floorboards, fireplaces and glass light fittings imported from England. Italian tiles add a distinctive touch of elegance to two beautifully finished bathrooms. Every detail has been considered with class and luxury in mind.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, the designer kitchen connects with spacious open-plan family living and dining, where large, double-glazed wooden sliding doors open to a deck enjoying a north-easterly aspect. It’s an inviting setting for morning coffee, long lunches and relaxed evenings overlooking the garden.\r\n\r\nAll three bedrooms are generous doubles. The master has its own sunroom, a lovely retreat for reading, a quiet sitting room or a light-filled study/office. A pull-down loft staircase provides access to approximately 80m² of dry storage, offering plenty of space to keep belongings neatly tucked away.\r\n\r\nThe spacious backyard offers wonderful possibilities. Currently a blank canvas, there’s room to explore adding a swimming pool, while still leaving space for entertaining, children and pets to play. With privacy from neighbouring homes, you can create your own garden sanctuary and enjoy outdoor living in peace.\r\n\r\nThe location is equally appealing, positioned roughly equidistant from Cheltenham Beach, the Vauxhall shops and Devonport Village. From local cafés and shops to the village’s waterfront, beach, ferry and everyday amenities, there is so much to enjoy so close to home.\r\n\r\nA carport and three additional off-street parking spaces complete the picture.\r\n\r\nBeautifully finished and quietly positioned along the slip road off Albert Road, this is a home to fall in love with, and a place to make your own.",
